WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:00.833
(audience clapping)

00:00:00.833 --> 00:00:02.291
- We're showing L.A. some real love,

00:00:02.291 --> 00:00:04.250
and while I admittedly don't know much

00:00:04.250 --> 00:00:05.653
about sports ball, it's known,

00:00:05.653 --> 00:00:09.523
you can't live in Los Angeles
and not embrace the Lakers.

00:00:09.523 --> 00:00:12.150
They're part of what makes
the heart of this city beat.

00:00:12.150 --> 00:00:13.340
I think everybody can agree on that.

00:00:13.340 --> 00:00:16.565
My next guest, actually,
is the owner of the team.

00:00:16.565 --> 00:00:19.740
Last year, she became the
first female controlling owner

00:00:19.740 --> 00:00:22.053
to lead an NBA team to a championship.

00:00:22.053 --> 00:00:23.037
(imitates trumpets)

00:00:23.037 --> 00:00:24.107
(audience cheering)

00:00:24.107 --> 00:00:27.470
Please welcome the leader Laker
nation, Jeanie Buss, y'all!

00:00:27.470 --> 00:00:32.470
(audience cheering)
(country music)

00:00:46.630 --> 00:00:47.633
Okay.

00:00:48.704 --> 00:00:50.250
So, meet the ladies,

00:00:50.250 --> 00:00:51.980
meet Kirby, meet Kristen.
- Hi!

00:00:51.980 --> 00:00:54.550
- The Queenpins looks fantastic!

00:00:54.550 --> 00:00:55.383
- Thank you.

00:00:55.383 --> 00:00:56.216
- You're a badass!

00:00:56.216 --> 00:00:57.300
I just want to lead with that.

00:00:57.300 --> 00:00:58.670
I'm very excited to have you here.

00:00:58.670 --> 00:01:00.140
But the Lakers are, you know,

00:01:00.140 --> 00:01:01.650
part of the glue that
holds the city together.

00:01:01.650 --> 00:01:03.150
Why do you think that is?

00:01:03.150 --> 00:01:07.340
- Well, you know, when my dad
bought the team back in 1979,

00:01:07.340 --> 00:01:10.630
it was really important to him
to give Los Angeles something

00:01:10.630 --> 00:01:12.758
that we could all rally together.

00:01:12.758 --> 00:01:16.030
And, what he did was,

00:01:16.030 --> 00:01:19.780
he built a team that Los
Angeles could, you know,

00:01:19.780 --> 00:01:23.180
be proud of under a purple and gold flag.

00:01:23.180 --> 00:01:27.232
And it was important for him
for everybody to feel included,

00:01:27.232 --> 00:01:29.280
to be Laker fans.

00:01:29.280 --> 00:01:30.840
And we're all has been at Laker game.

00:01:30.840 --> 00:01:33.765
Could you see, a Hollywood
legend, like Jack Nicholson-

00:01:33.765 --> 00:01:35.450
- I always see, he loves it!
- Sitting there

00:01:35.450 --> 00:01:36.850
with regular fans-
- Yeah.

00:01:36.850 --> 00:01:37.890
- Enjoying the game.

00:01:37.890 --> 00:01:40.940
- Yeah, but let's talk about
your role as a female owner.

00:01:40.940 --> 00:01:42.420
That is so cool.

00:01:42.420 --> 00:01:44.040
I'm so proud of you and
I don't even know you,

00:01:44.040 --> 00:01:44.873
but I do know.

00:01:44.873 --> 00:01:46.438
(audience cheering)
But I think it's so cool!

00:01:46.438 --> 00:01:50.753
- But for me, the first thing
that I thought was like,

00:01:50.753 --> 00:01:53.080
who's going to be the next female

00:01:53.080 --> 00:01:54.750
to do something like this?
- Yeah.

00:01:54.750 --> 00:01:57.300
- You know, because I
know what it meant to me

00:01:57.300 --> 00:01:59.927
to see women in powerful positions.

00:01:59.927 --> 00:02:02.081
That inspired me.

00:02:02.081 --> 00:02:02.914
- Yeah.

00:02:02.914 --> 00:02:04.510
- And, you know, as a matter of fact,

00:02:04.510 --> 00:02:08.630
it's important that not
only we see women leading,

00:02:08.630 --> 00:02:10.600
but that women can lead men.

00:02:10.600 --> 00:02:12.804
And so the fact that the
Lakers is a men's team.

00:02:12.804 --> 00:02:15.755
(audience clapping)
It's really important.

00:02:15.755 --> 00:02:16.740
- That's so true.

00:02:16.740 --> 00:02:18.633
So, we can't talk about the Lakers

00:02:18.633 --> 00:02:20.720
without mentioning Kobe
Bryant. Who was here.

00:02:20.720 --> 00:02:22.610
I love him. I fell in love
with him even in person.

00:02:22.610 --> 00:02:24.960
And you know, that wasn't one of those

00:02:24.960 --> 00:02:27.070
huge things to me, even if you
didn't know him personally,

00:02:27.070 --> 00:02:28.080
it really did hit.

00:02:28.080 --> 00:02:30.110
I remember being in my house
and we finding out the news,

00:02:30.110 --> 00:02:31.737
like, it hit everyone.

00:02:31.737 --> 00:02:34.330
And that's how powerful
I do think that sports

00:02:34.330 --> 00:02:35.663
and those figures can be for kids

00:02:35.663 --> 00:02:38.940
or adults and that excitement
in that place in time.

00:02:38.940 --> 00:02:42.120
And I don't know how. And he
really supported you. I heard.

00:02:42.120 --> 00:02:43.807
So how, that must've been really hard

00:02:43.807 --> 00:02:45.472
to come back from as a team.

00:02:45.472 --> 00:02:48.170
- Yeah. I mean, you know, I mean,

00:02:48.170 --> 00:02:50.916
we all lost somebody
that was really special.

00:02:50.916 --> 00:02:55.916
It's left a void in my life
and a void for all Laker fans.

00:02:56.501 --> 00:03:01.501
And, you know, I remember
when my dad passed in 2013,

00:03:02.630 --> 00:03:03.828
Kobe reached out to me

00:03:03.828 --> 00:03:07.249
and invited me to have lunch
with him in Orange County.

00:03:07.249 --> 00:03:11.570
And, he brought his daughter
Gianna along with them.

00:03:11.570 --> 00:03:13.560
And he said, I hope you don't mind.

00:03:13.560 --> 00:03:15.270
I brought Gianna with me

00:03:15.270 --> 00:03:19.225
because I wanted him to see a
woman in a position of power

00:03:19.225 --> 00:03:22.460
and hear what you had to say.

00:03:22.460 --> 00:03:23.576
- Yeah.

00:03:23.576 --> 00:03:24.409
- And I know what he was doing,

00:03:24.409 --> 00:03:26.220
was really motivating me

00:03:26.220 --> 00:03:29.860
because, you know, there's
all these little girls

00:03:29.860 --> 00:03:31.880
that are looking up to a person like me,

00:03:31.880 --> 00:03:33.045
in my position.

00:03:33.045 --> 00:03:36.259
And, you know, that's the
kind of thing that Kobe did,

00:03:36.259 --> 00:03:38.059
would motivate,

00:03:38.059 --> 00:03:42.750
He knew how to motivate
people and to remind me

00:03:42.750 --> 00:03:45.350
of how important what I'm doing is,

00:03:45.350 --> 00:03:49.040
and through that, we
can honor Kobe's memory.

00:03:49.040 --> 00:03:51.139
And that's how we keep his legacy alive.

00:03:51.139 --> 00:03:52.600
(audience clapping)

00:03:52.600 --> 00:03:54.870
- It was interesting for people like me,

00:03:54.870 --> 00:03:56.930
like, I met him on this show.

00:03:56.930 --> 00:03:58.340
He came on and it was so funny,

00:03:58.340 --> 00:04:00.140
cause I don't know a lot about sports,

00:04:00.140 --> 00:04:02.569
but all we did was talk
about his daughters.

00:04:02.569 --> 00:04:04.220
And we talked about his wife,

00:04:04.220 --> 00:04:06.470
and we talked about family
stuff, and he's a writer,

00:04:06.470 --> 00:04:08.230
and we just talked about
something completely different.

00:04:08.230 --> 00:04:10.240
So, I knew him differently than most,

00:04:10.240 --> 00:04:11.940
but you can tell he's just so charismatic

00:04:11.940 --> 00:04:13.610
and had so much pride in his girls.

00:04:13.610 --> 00:04:17.080
And, it was just really cool
how he was pushing, you know,

00:04:17.080 --> 00:04:18.710
all the right people in the right places.

00:04:18.710 --> 00:04:19.680
I felt like that was really cool.

00:04:19.680 --> 00:04:21.050
It was true of his character. I think.

00:04:21.050 --> 00:04:21.940
- Exactly.

00:04:21.940 --> 00:04:25.410
And I saw that episode
and I say to all Kobe fans

00:04:25.410 --> 00:04:27.260
and Kelly fans to watch that episode,

00:04:27.260 --> 00:04:31.090
because you guys really
had a nice connection and-

00:04:31.090 --> 00:04:32.300
- Well, he told me he married a tourist

00:04:32.300 --> 00:04:33.885
and I was like, good luck.

00:04:33.885 --> 00:04:35.620
I was like, your wife's a tourist?

00:04:35.620 --> 00:04:36.696
Oh man, that's a fun house.

00:04:36.696 --> 00:04:38.846
(laughs)

00:04:38.846 --> 00:04:41.030
It was just really fun to get to know him,

00:04:41.030 --> 00:04:43.050
'cause I would not, really, have known him

00:04:43.050 --> 00:04:44.540
other than this show and to find out

00:04:44.540 --> 00:04:45.590
how much he really pushed you

00:04:45.590 --> 00:04:47.610
because most people would look at a female

00:04:47.610 --> 00:04:48.560
owner of a team and go,

00:04:48.560 --> 00:04:50.420
oh, she owns a women's basketball team.

00:04:50.420 --> 00:04:51.253
- Right, right.

00:04:51.253 --> 00:04:53.634
- You know, most people would
think that, unfortunately.

00:04:53.634 --> 00:04:55.310
- Well, as a matter of fact,

00:04:55.310 --> 00:04:59.059
when the WNBA was founded back in 97,

00:04:59.059 --> 00:05:01.520
the commissioner went to my dad and said,

00:05:01.520 --> 00:05:04.160
well, I assume Jeanie's
going to run the team.

00:05:04.160 --> 00:05:05.880
And my dad said to him, no,

00:05:05.880 --> 00:05:08.226
Jeanie is going to run the Lakers someday.

00:05:08.226 --> 00:05:11.520
(audience cheering)
- I love your dad.

00:05:11.520 --> 00:05:12.682
That's so awesome!

00:05:12.682 --> 00:05:14.490
(audience cheering)

00:05:14.490 --> 00:05:17.700
It's so awesome and so
supportive, and so cool.

00:05:17.700 --> 00:05:18.550
What a great dad!

